# Patch: BUG-002 — Replace hardcoded metric with placeholder

## Bug
`templates/narrative_report.md` line 30 had `metric: 73.5%` (concrete number without source:)  
in the traceability rule illustration.

## Root Cause
The example in the "Traceability rule" section used a concrete number to demonstrate format.

## Fix
Replaced concrete example values with placeholders:
```diff
-metric: 73.5%
-source: experiments/r-001/metrics/eval_results.json:line_42
-paper:  Table 3, row "Ours (KPConv)"
-gap:    -0.4 pp (within ±0.5 pp tolerance)
+metric: [METRIC]
+source: experiments/<run_id>/raw_metrics.json:line_<N>
+paper:  Table X, row "..."
+gap:    ±X.X pp (within ±TOLERANCE_MIOU tolerance)
```

## Verification
```
$ grep -n 'metric:' templates/narrative_report.md | head -5
(metric: [METRIC] — no concrete number)
```

## Rollback
Restore concrete example values in the traceability rule illustration section.
